   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 500eb (Expensive) <strong>♦</strong> <strong>I</strong>nstall: Clinic</p>\n<p><strong>Humanity Loss:</strong> 3 (1d6)</p>\n<p><em>Made in the U.K. 50 years ago, this optical upgrade enables cybereyes to be swapped as easily as cyberlimbs.</em></p>\n<p>Cybereye Option. Cybereyes can be installed into an open Quick Swap Socket or uninstalled with an Action. The first time you install a new Cybereye, whether using a Quick Swap Socket or otherwise, you always accrue Humanity Loss. Reattaching one you've already used before with a Quick Swap Socket does not do this.</p>\n<p><strong>Type:</strong> Cybereye<br>\n<strong>Install:</strong> Clinic<br>\n<strong>Option Slots:</strong> uses 1</p>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Cyberware &gt; Cyberoptics).</em></p>"
